Exists returns nil when errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) and otherwise wraps the
os.Stat error with %w. A bare fs.ErrNotExist never leaves os.Stat (it is a
*fs.PathError around a syscall.Errno, whose Is method decides), so the syscall
origins stay, wrapped by *fs.PathError.Unwrap and fmt.Errorf "source: stat: %w", and
marked "possibly handled" (custom Is). fs.ErrNotExist itself must not be listed.
-fanout 0 keeps the entries ungrouped so that chains and guard marks are visible.
-- args --
-fanout 0 source/source.go:@exists
